    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize feedback by flagging misconceptions (e.g., ‘You mixed up x² vs. 2x’). For conceptual gaps, they might generate analogies or visualizations dynamically. However, risk is over-reliance; teachers should use them as tools to guide rather than replace direct instruction. My low extraversion suggests I’d appreciate AI’s one-on-one tutoring but need human validation afterward."
